WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.040
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week on
Game of Thrones it was throw down time. The

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.970
episode was directed by Neil Marshall, the
guy who directed the Season 2 Blackwater episode

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.070
so if it felt like a sequel, that's why. And
it was so awesome. Before we get going round

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.309
9 of the giveaway starts now.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.599
Just as a way to say thank you to all you
guys for being so awesome I'm picking a random

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:22.519
subscriber from the comments to give an amazon
gift card to. Like normal I'll announce the

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:25.439
winner in my Q&amp;A video tomorrow night.

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:31.119
So much to talk about so let's just get in
it. I'm going to do my top 5 moments, then

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:35.720
review and then I'll circle back around for
any other plot threads we need to remember.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.600
So careful for spoilers from the episode if
you haven't seen it yet. But here we go. Number

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.730
5 - Maester Aemon Explains Love

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.980
Even for a Targaryen Maester Aemon was on
fire tonight. In fact, he was my favorite

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.770
supporting character. Alliser Thorne got a
pretty good battle speech, but I feel like

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:54.200
Aemon's speech about love was better.
If you're not familiar with him, he was the

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.020
great uncle of the Mad King. When his older
brothers died they offered him the crown but

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.650
he turned them down and took the black. That's
what he was talking about when he said he

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.250
was at court and women were throwing themselves
at him.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.810
I couldn't find out who specifically the woman
he loved might have been or which house she

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.759
belonged to, but if you know be sure to write
it in the comments.

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:17.359
I like how he foreshadowed Ygritte and Jon
Snow's reunion with his big takeaway quote

00:01:17.359 --> 00:01:22.240
"love is the death of duty". Their duty was
to chop each other's heads off, but because

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.460
they were still in love they just forgot about
it when the time came.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.780
I also love how well that theme of unending
love works thematically with the threat of

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.439
the white walkers and necromancy. Like if
Jon hadn't told Samwell to burn the bodies

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:39.350
at the end. His and Ygritte's love might turn
into zombie wight love and LITERALLY become

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:39.840
undying.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.469
I didn't see Maester Aemon during the battle,
so fingers crossed that he survived to the

00:01:44.469 --> 00:01:44.929
finale.

00:01:44.929 --> 00:01:48.399
Number 4 - Jon Snow Explains What it is to
Be In Love

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.600
I don't believe for a minute he's not a bloody
poet. This whole gossipy exchange would have

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.030
been a really funny scene in any other episode.
But because this episode was like Two Towers

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.069
and the battle of Helm's Deep it was very
wishful. Samwell did get a few moments with

00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:03.530
Gilly, and they have their own kind of love.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.579
But really, it did seem like he just wanted
to know what it was like having sex.

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:10.500
I love how hard his brain was working to find
a way past their oath so he could hook up

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.520
with Gilly and not feel guilty about it. To
be fair, Night's Watch brothers have broken

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.440
the implied no-sex oath all the time over
the years. I say implied just because Sam

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.450
was correct in his literal interpretation
of the Oath.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.690
Really though, he should just go for it. But
I have a feeling if anything does go down

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.060
between them, Gilly will be the first one
to make a move.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.390
Number 3 - The Wildlings Attack On Two Fronts

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.650
Jon was correct when he was saying Mance was
just testing their Northern defenses. They

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.610
have a whole lot more giants where those two
came from. The giant lifting the gate reminded

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.480
me of Return of the Jedi when the Rancor died.
They killed that one giant and the other one

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.600
flipped out. That wasn't the only Return of
the Jedi reference I saw either.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.120
This episode was a little bit Two Towers mixed
with a little bit Star Wars and a little bit

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.560
Star Trek. The way they altered the theme
song for the battle made it so much cooler.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.470
If you didn't notice, it was just this off
tempo version of the opening credits theme

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.770
song that started when Jon Snow jumped down
and start swinging longclaw around.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:08.380
It also seemed like the whole episode was
drums and string basses.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:12.340
That early shot when the raiding party was
rushing the South Gate gave us that amazing

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:17.570
panoramic shot that went from them, panned
up the wall to and out over Mance's army.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.080
Just to hammer home that Mance was attacking
from the North and the raiders from the south

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.260
at the same time.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.490
I'm hoping they give us a big daylight shot
of Mance's entire army, just to give you an

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:31.020
idea for scale. Because the Night's Watch
only had about a 100 men before tonight's

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.260
battle. So they're probably down to about
50 or 60. The gate is still intact though.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.890
But if one giant could lift it up it's not
much comfort.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.290
Number 2 - Jon Snow takes Command

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.250
This was like Jon's Kobayashi Maru, the unwinnable
scenario. That's why I mentioned Star Trek

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.950
before. I'll go so far as to say that the
scenario is still playing out. Because at

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:54.520
the end of the episode he has to deal with
a fight they definitely can't win.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.860
I loved how Dolorous Edd invented a reason
for Janos Slynt to go back down. I kind of

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.690
half expected them to just punch him and make
him pass out. It's like the show is preparing

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:04.920
us for Jon Snow to take a leadership role.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.170
Janos Slynt is the only other senior commander
left alive so it's unclear whether or not

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:14.670
Jon will take full command of the night's
watch next week or if it will turn into a

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.479
big plot that will carry over into season
5.

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:20.560
One of my favorite moments was when the brother's
on top of the wall asked Jon how he knew the

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.770
climbers wouldn't get to the top till morning.
"Because I made that climb".

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:28.270
and my Number 1 moment of course - Ygritte
Dies

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:33.419
The way Jon just smiled at her was so amazing.
That was my favorite reaction shot of the

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:37.990
episode. I'm not sure if he was thinking about
the strung arrow she had on him but this is

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:42.189
where Maester Aemon's quote came full circle.
They both just kind of freeze.

00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:45.009
I totally did not see that little kid coming.
I actually thought they were going to let

00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:50.539
him kill that big Thenn in like a revenge
moment. But that's why Game of Thrones is

00:04:50.539 --> 00:04:54.210
so awesome. Now Jon gets to feel extra guilty
about Ygritte's death because he's the one

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:54.590
that told that little boy to start killing
people.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.830
Which is probably what drove him to the decision
to walk into the dragon's maw that is Mance's

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.530
army. Without his sword.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:06.199
It's so sad to see Ygritte go, but did anyone
think they were not a tragic couple? It's

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:10.729
like relationships and especially weddings
equal death on the show. So maybe Sam is better

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:12.999
off not knowing what sex is like.

00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:17.120
I definitely think the rest of Jon's heart
died tonight though. He's frozen solid to

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:22.099
the core. I think it will be his sense of
duty that will keep him going. He will probably

00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:24.639
never laugh out loud or smile again though.

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:28.719
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
biggest WTF moment was.

00:05:28.719 --> 00:05:33.949
I feel like we're all thinking the same unfortunate
ginger thoughts right now though. Her last

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:36.999
line, you know nothing Jon Snow. Is straight
off the page from her death in the book.

00:05:36.999 --> 00:05:42.020
If you want to read her death scene in the
book it's in Book 3 Jon Chapter 7.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:49.020
Overall the episode was A plus from a production
stand point. It really was like a mini recreation

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:56.819
of the battle for Helm's Deep in Two Towers,
from the way they altered the music to the

00:05:56.819 --> 00:06:01.759
Wildlings Charging. Very cinematic and very
awesome. Don't be surprised if this episode

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:06.419
gets nominated for a technical emmy. Those
are the emmys they give for production.

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:10.099
Like I said Neil Marshall directed the episode,
he was the person who did Blackwater in season

00:06:10.099 --> 00:06:15.439
2. Which was also kind of like a Helm's Deep
story, Helm's Deep with Wildfire.

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:19.849
Just comparing the two episodes, I think from
a production standpoint and emotional payoff,

00:06:19.849 --> 00:06:25.240
Blackwater is still my favorite. Kit Harington
is awesome, but almost no one on the show

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.219
can hold a candle to Peter Dinklage.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:32.409
I guess during Blackwater, Joffrey was their
Janos Slynt. Like the person in charge who

00:06:32.409 --> 00:06:33.949
is also the biggest coward.

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:38.629
Just because I think Blackwater was a little
better doesn't mean this episode was bad.

00:06:38.629 --> 00:06:42.809
I just feel like they're holding something
really big back for the finale. So you leave

00:06:42.809 --> 00:06:46.460
this episode feeling like you got half a story.
It was a freaking awesome half of a story

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.050
though.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:55.050
Did anyone else think of Jabba's Gate in Return
of the Jedi when Jon went to meet with Mance?

00:06:56.539 --> 00:06:58.449
Like he's Luke Skywalker waiting outside Jabba's
Palace without his lightsaber.

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:01.039
I wonder if they shot it to look that way
on purpose?

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:06.360
I'm really curious which moment they'll end
the season on. There's a lot of big plots

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.020
still floating in the air.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.069
I'll leave a lot of the other plot discussion
for my Q&amp;A video tomorrow, but here are a

00:07:11.069 --> 00:07:13.849
few things they left hanging in this episode.

00:07:13.849 --> 00:07:18.059
What the hell is Jon going to do when he gets
to Mance's camp? I don't think anyone believes

00:07:18.059 --> 00:07:22.749
he's going to be able to kill him. Janos Slynt
is still an issue. They mostly used him for

00:07:22.749 --> 00:07:26.740
comedy in this episode. But he's been a pain
in Jon's ass all season.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:30.319
And what are they going to do with Tormund
Giantsbane. He's one of the wildlings best

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:35.490
fighters. There's no way he's going to give
up information. Unless it's tips on having

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:39.059
sex with bears. That really was one of the
funniest parts of the episode.

00:07:39.059 --> 00:07:44.289
So feel free to ask any remaining plot questions
for the finale, please use spoiler tags if

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.879
you've read the books and want to talk about
book 4 and 5 stuff. My Q&amp;A will post tomorrow

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:48.029
like normal. Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:48.029 --> 00:07:51.499
Because next week is the finale I'm going
to be doing more bonus videos than normal

00:07:51.499 --> 00:07:54.930
later this week and through the next couple
of weeks. My next one will probably be ranking

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.839
all of the previous finales. I'll try to post
that by Thursday.

